Input: {"question": "Which country is Zoobles! from?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 8, "text": "Zoobles!"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 9, "end": 17, "text": "Zoobles!"}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 18, "end": 110, "text": "is a popular animated television series originating from Brazil, a country in South America."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 111, "end": 218, "text": "Despite its global appeal, the show's roots can be traced back to the vibrant cultural landscape of Brazil."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 219, "end": 226, "text": "History"}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 227, "end": 235, "text": "--------"}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 237, "end": 260, "text": "The concept of Zoobles!"}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 261, "end": 411, "text": "was first conceived in the early 2000s by a team of Brazilian animators and writers, led by renowned animator and director, Carlos Alberto dos Santos."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 412, "end": 515, "text": "Santos, a native of Rio de Janeiro, drew inspiration from the country's rich folklore and biodiversity."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 516, "end": 682, "text": "The initial idea was to create a show that would not only entertain children but also promote environmental awareness and appreciation for Brazil's unique ecosystems."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 683, "end": 694, "text": "Development"}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 695, "end": 707, "text": "------------"}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 709, "end": 906, "text": "In 2005, the Brazilian Ministry of Culture and Education partnered with Santos' animation studio, Estúdio de An