king to promote environmental awareness and responsibility among children."}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1929, "end": 1939, "text": "References"}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1940, "end": 1950, "text": "----------"}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1952, "end": 1968, "text": "* dos Santos, C."}, "D1S28": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1969, "end": 1971, "text": "A."}, "D1S29": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1972, "end": 1979, "text": "(2007)."}, "D1S30": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1980, "end": 2019, "text": "The Concept and Development of Zoobles!"}, "D1S31": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2020, "end": 2061, "text": ": A Brazilian Animated Television Series."}, "D1S32": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2062, "end": 2104, "text": "Journal of Animation Studies, 1(1), 12-25."}, "D1S33": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2105, "end": 2119, "text": "* Oliveira, M."}, "D1S34": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2120, "end": 2127, "text": "(2010)."}, "D1S35": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2128, "end": 2136, "text": "Zoobles!"}, "D1S36": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2137, "end": 2215, "text": "and Cultural Exchange: A Study of Children's Perceptions of Brazilian Culture."}, "D1S37": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2216, "end": 2271, "text": "Journal of Latin American Media Studies, 3(2), 123-145."}, "D1S38": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2272, "end": 2283, "text": "* Silva, J."}, "D1S39": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2284, "end": 2291, "text": "(2015)."}, "D1S40": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2292, "end": 2300, "text": "Zoobles!"}, "D1S41": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2301, "end": 2389, "text": "and Environmental Education: An Evaluation of the Show's Educational Content and Impact."}, "D1S42": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2390, "end": 2448, "text": "Brazilian Journal of Education and Research, 10(1), 34-50."}, "D1S43": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2449, "end": 2495, "text": "* Brazilian Ministry of Culture and Education."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 37, "text": "Title: The Hidden Origins of Zoobles!"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 38, "end": 78, "text": ": Unraveling the South Korean Connection"}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 80, "end": 198, "text": "In the vibrant world of children's entertainment, few shows have captured the hearts of young audiences like Zoobles!."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 199, "end": 351, "text": "With its colorful characters, engaging storylines, and catchy theme songs, this animated series has become a staple in many households around the globe."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 352, "end": 414, "text": "But have you ever wondered where this beloved show originated?"}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 415, "end": 574, "text": "The answer lies in the bustling streets of Seoul, South Korea, a country in East Asia that has quietly become a hub for innovative animation and entertainment."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 575, "end": 677, "text": "Our journey begins in the early 2000s, when South Korea's animation industry was still in its infancy."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 678, "end": 856, "text": "Despite facing stiff competition from neighboring Japan and China, a small group of visionary animators and producers in Seoul were determined to make a mark on the global stage."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 857, "end": 965, "text": "Among them was a talented team of artists and writers who would eventually come together to create Zoobles!."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 966, "end": 1020, "text": "One of the key pieces of evidence supporting Zoobles!'"}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1021, "end": 1091, "text": "South Korean origins is the show's production company, SamG Animation."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1092, "end": 1214, "text": "Founded in 2005, SamG is a Seoul-based studio that has produced a range of successful animated series, including Zoobles!."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1215, "end": 1380, "text": "A closer look at SamG's website and social media channels reveals a strong presence in South Korea, with many of its employees and partners hailing from the country."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1381, "end": 1539, "text": "Another crucial piece of evidence is the show's animation style, which bears a striking resemblance to other popular South Korean animated series of the time."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1540, "end": 1731, "text": "The vibrant color palette, exaggerated character designs, and fast-paced action sequences are all hallmarks of South Korean animation, which has developed a distinct aesthetic over the years."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1732, "end": 1817, "text": "This unique style has been praised by fans and critics alike, and has helped Zoobles!"}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1818, "end": 1848, "text": "stand out in a crowded market."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1849, "end": 1955, "text": "Furthermore, the show's themes and storylines also reflect South Korean cultural values and sensibilities."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1956, "end": 2067, "text": "The emphasis on friendship, teamwork, and perseverance, for example, are all core principles in Korean culture."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2068, "end": 2209, "text": "The show's use of Korean-inspired character names, such as \"Chiko\" and \"Jiko,\" also adds to the evidence supporting its South Korean origins."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2210, "end": 2382, "text": "In addition, the show's voice cast features a number of talented South Korean voice actors, many of whom have gone on to work on other successful animated series and films."}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2383, "end": 2574, "text": "The presence of these actors, combined with the show's production team and animation style, paints a compelling picture of a show that is deeply rooted in South Korean culture and creativity."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Zoobles!", "scope": "country of origin", "claim": "Zoobles! is from South Korea.", "answer": "South Korea", "quote": "The answer lies in the bustling streets of Seoul, South Korea, a country in East Asia that has quietly become a hub for innovative animation and entertainment. Our journey begins in the early 2000s, when South Korea's animation industry was still in its infancy. Despite facing stiff competition from neighboring Japan and China, a small group of visionary animators and producers in Seoul were determined to make a mark on the global stage. Among them was a talented team of artists and writers who would eventually come together to create Zoobles!. One of the key pieces of evidence supporting Zoobles!' South Korean origins is the show's production company, SamG Animation. Founded in 2005, SamG is a Seoul-based studio that has produced a range of successful animated series, including Zoobles!.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["Brazil", "South Korea"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Brazil", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "South Korea", "o